/client-sdk-cpp/pull/300\r\n* Update actions/upload-artifact action to v7.0.2 by @renovate[bot] in https://github.com/livekit/client-sdk-cpp/pull/302\r\n* Proper Linux compiler support/documentation by @alan-george-lk in https://github.com/livekit/client-sdk-cpp/pull/303\r\n* Update Rust SDK to FFI 0.13.4 release commit by @stephen-derosa in https://github.com/livekit/client-sdk-cpp/pull/306\r\n\r\n## New Contributors\r\n* @mdepinet made their first contribution in https://github.com/livekit/client-sdk-cpp/pull/300\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/livekit/client-sdk-cpp/compare/v1.13.0...v1.13.1\r\n\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\n### Minor Changes as of `v1.13.0`\r\n\r\n* [`livekit-capture`](https://github.com/livekit/rust-sdks/tree/main/livekit-capture) crate support\r\n  * LiveKit Capture allows capture sources to be owned by the SDK. The chosen capture backend \"pumps\" frames directly within the Rust core, bypassing FFI overhead and management of raw frames by applications.\r\n  * Currently supported backends: `GStreamer` and simulated pattern/clock source types\r\n  * Capture is opt-in. See the `-capture` releases below, or build using the `--capture` build flag, and optional source type arguments\r\n  * [C++ SDK documentation](https://github.com/livekit/client-sdk-cpp/blob/main/docs/capture-sources.md)\r\n\r\n> [!WARNING]\r\n> As of `v1.12.3`, the \"linux\" release artifacts are now removed. Please move to the `ubuntu-24.04` labeled version which is functionally equivalent.","mentions_count":4}